# Kreel-Lok Nomad

## Lore

The kreel-lok are an aquatic race of intelligent creatures from another dimension - a giant fish with two human-like arms, sometimes mistaken for a Devil Shark with tragic results, since they are generally gentle and peace-loving.

Many were accidentally Rifted to Earth after the Great Cataclysm, and over the centuries they have multiplied into nomadic communities found all over the world. Relatively harmless as they are, they will resort to violence to resist encroachment. Lately the naut''yll have enslaved them in such numbers that almost forty percent of all kreel-lok on Rifts Earth are now slaves.

They live in a simple, open, cooperative society with a strong sense of camaraderie - food, supplies, weapons, equipment and defences are all shared. Males are generally the craftsmen, hunters and protectors; females have an equal place and, though seldom warriors, may take any occupation including magic.

## GM Notes

Smaller communities keep no permanent villages. Like dolphins and whales they travel in pods of ten to a hundred, sheltering in sunken wrecks, caves and reefs, or simply swimming, playing, hunting and sleeping in open water with male protectors taking turns on watch.

Large communities run from a thousand to a hundred thousand, and build underwater barges towed along as shelter and storage. They cache weapons, food and supplies along familiar migration routes. They never build anything permanent; the ocean is their home.

Dolphins and whales often live with or travel near them as faithful allies. Sea turtles and other large animals are occasionally used as work animals or pets, and are never mistreated.

Toward surface dwellers there is real hostility. Surface people abuse what the kreel-lok regard as their fishing waters, and many humans and D-bees think them monsters and kill them out of fear or for sport. Hunted now by the naut''yll and occasionally the Splugorth, they often feel they have few friends - Tritonia and Lemuria being among the handful of human communities that have managed a real alliance.
